<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Matsya Union</h1><p class="st-meta">1948 CE – 1949 CE · capital Alwar</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A union of four princely states of eastern Rajputana, named after the ancient Matsya kingdom, which lasted from 1948 to 1949.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In March 1948 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/alwar-state">Alwar State</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bharatpur-state">Bharatpur State</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dholpur-state">Dholpur State</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/karauli-state">Karauli</a> were merged into the United State of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/matsya">Matsya</a>, named after the Matsya kingdom of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahabharata">Mahabharata</a>, which had lain in the same region. Alwar was the capital.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Maharaj Rana <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/udaybhan-singh">Udaybhan Singh</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dholpur-state">Dholpur</a> was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajpramukh">Rajpramukh</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shobha-ram">Shobha Ram</a> led the government. The union was formed shortly after Alwar's ruler had been suspected of links to the extremists behind <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahatma-gandhi">Gandhi's</a> assassination, which hastened central intervention.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After a short existence the Matsya Union was merged into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-state-of-rajasthan">United State of Rajasthan</a> in May 1949.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/matsya-union.jpg" alt="Matsya Union" width="320" height="329"><figcaption>Image: Photo Division, Government of India · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:N.V._Gadgil_at_Bharatpur_Railway_Station_for_the_inauguration_of_the_Matsya_States_Union_(March_1948).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1948 CE – 1949 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Alwar</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Udaybhan Singh, Shobha Ram</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism; Islam (Meo)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Mewati, Braj Bhasha, Hindi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>United State of Matsya</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1948&amp;focus=matsya-union" aria-label="Matsya Union on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6692 1167 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Matsya Union lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7012 1423L7018 1386M7012 1423L6996 1446M7012 1423L7038 1435M7012 1423L7031 1461M7012 1423L7012 1423M7012 1423L7053 1454"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7018 1386h0M6996 1446h0M7038 1435h0M7031 1461h0M7012 1423h0M7053 1454h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7012 1423h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7012 1423h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Alwar. <a href="/atlas?year=1948&amp;focus=matsya-union">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
